<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Costanera Q1 net flat at $15 mln.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Costanera Q1 net flat at $15 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to March 31.</p>
<p>EPS $0.11 vs vs $0.11</p>
<p>ADR $1.11 vs $1.11</p>
<p>Net $15 million vs $15 million</p>
<p>Revs $86.3 million vs 85.9 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Central Costanera SA, one of Argentina's two biggest thermoelectric generating companies, said at March 31 its net worth stood at $386 million.</p>
<p>The controlling 51 percent stake in Central Costanera is owned by Chile's ENDESA, which in turn is controlled by Chile's ENERSIS SA.</p>
<p>((-Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
</text>
